---
/**
 * AIGC Content Creation  ·  /solutions/ai-production/content
 *
 * AI copywriting and content production at studio scale, with human
 * strategists running every brief. Drawn from the source page's
 * strategy-first framing and the three content categories the studio
 * actually ships.
 *
 * Per repo standards: no em-dashes (U+2014), no decorative numerals inside
 * cards or repeated blocks, body copy at var(--type-body), hubStudio keeps
 * its canonical lowercase-h casing.
 */
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Button from '../../../components/Button.astro';

const colourBar = [
  '#e94e1b', '#c73e10', '#1e3a8a', '#0e1f4e', '#0e1633',
  '#6b6b73', '#a8a299', '#d8d3cb', '#e5e1db', '#ffffff',
];

const reasons = [
  {
    label: 'Infinite iterations',
    title: 'Test messaging angles without burning writer bandwidth.',
    body: 'Run a dozen tones, formats and angles before the campaign goes live. The first version is no longer the only version the team can afford. Iteration becomes a strategy lever rather than a budget item.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Speed without sacrifice',
    title: 'Launch campaigns at the pace of culture, not the calendar.',
    body: 'Fill content calendars, respond to market moments and ship new variants in days, not weeks. The bottleneck moves from production to strategy, which is where it belonged in the first place.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Personalised at scale',
    title: 'Different personas, markets and journey stages, same voice.',
    body: 'Variants for persona, channel, market and stage of journey while keeping the brand voice consistent. Hyper-personalised content stops being a luxury the budget cannot afford.',
  },
];

const lanes = [
  {
    label: 'Brand & campaign',
    heading: 'Brand and campaign content.',
    image: '/Images/pr-hero.jpg',
    alt: 'A daylit editorial review with campaign storyboards and bylined articles pinned beside a calibrated monitor showing a brand narrative draft, warm shadow grade.',
    lead: 'Campaign concepting, PR and editorial, video and social scripts. The headline-grade work, faster.',
    body: [
      "Campaign narratives, visual storyboards with scene descriptions, multi-channel messaging frameworks, concept testing at speed. Press releases, thought leadership, industry reports and brand storytelling. Video scripts for product launches, social calendars and platform-specific captions.",
      'Useful where the campaign needs to ship in many places at the same time, in a voice that holds across channels and registers.',
    ],
    tags: [
      'Campaign concepting', 'Visual storyboards',
      'PR & editorial', 'Thought leadership',
      'Video scripts', 'Social calendars',
      'TikTok / Reels scripting',
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Commercial & performance',
    heading: 'Commercial and performance content.',
    image: '/Images/hub4presentation.jpg',
    alt: 'A daylit performance content review with PDP copy variations, email sequences and landing page drafts pinned beside a calibrated monitor, lifted black point, real-photography grade.',
    lead: 'E-commerce, email and CRM, website and landing pages. The content that closes the loop.',
    body: [
      "Product descriptions optimised for conversion, category copy, A+ content, marketplace-specific content for Amazon, Tmall and Shopify. Email campaign sequences, welcome flows, abandoned-cart recovery, behaviour-triggered personalisation, subject-line and preview-text testing.",
      'Useful where the channel has a measurable goal and the content has a measurable job. The PDP, the email, the landing page, all built for the conversion they exist to drive.',
    ],
    tags: [
      'Product descriptions', 'Category page copy',
      'A+ content', 'Amazon / Tmall / Shopify',
      'Email sequences', 'Welcome flows',
      'Subject-line testing', 'Landing-page copy',
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Strategic & naming',
    heading: 'Strategic and naming content.',
    image: '/Images/ms-hero.jpg',
    alt: 'A documentary in-studio frame of a strategist reviewing brand naming explorations and tone-of-voice frameworks on a calibrated monitor, warm window light, real-photography grade.',
    lead: 'Naming exploration, tone-of-voice frameworks, SEO and content strategy. The strategic spine.',
    body: [
      "Product and service naming, tagline and positioning, brand voice guidelines and tone frameworks. Messaging architecture and key messages. SEO-optimised blog and pillar content, keyword-rich category descriptions, meta description and title-tag optimisation, content briefs and editorial calendars.",
      'Useful where the work upstream of every campaign needs to be sharper than what AI alone will return. The strategic layer is human; the execution layer scales around it.',
    ],
    tags: [
      'Naming exploration', 'Tagline and positioning',
      'Tone of voice', 'Messaging architecture',
      'SEO pillar content', 'Meta description / title tag',
      'Content briefs', 'Editorial calendars',
    ],
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How does AI content creation compare to traditional copywriting?',
    a: 'AI-powered content excels at high-volume, structured work: product descriptions, email sequences, social captions at unprecedented speed and cost-efficiency. Traditional copywriting remains ideal for nuanced brand manifestos and highly conceptual work. Our human-led AI approach delivers strategic depth and operational scale.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What types of content work best with AIGC?',
    a: 'Product descriptions, email campaigns, social media content, video scripts, SEO articles, press releases and campaign storyboards perform exceptionally well. AIGC is particularly powerful for creating variations, testing messaging angles and adapting content across channels and markets.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does it take to produce AI-generated content?',
    a: 'Simple content batches (product descriptions, social posts) ship in 24 to 48 hours. Complex projects such as campaign storyboards or thought leadership typically take 3 to 5 days including strategy and refinement. Significant time savings versus traditional copywriting workflows.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you only generate content, or can you adapt existing brand materials?',
    a: 'Both. We create entirely new content from strategy briefs, or work from existing material to generate variations, adaptations and extensions. We also specialise in transcreating content across languages while maintaining brand voice and cultural relevance.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you handle brand voice consistency?',
    a: 'We train custom language models on the brand guidelines, existing content and approved messaging. Our strategists review every piece to ensure voice consistency, and the quality control process verifies alignment with the brand standard before delivery.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you price content generation projects?',
    a: 'Pricing depends on complexity, volume, customisation and the strategic input needed. Simple product descriptions operate at different price points than campaign storyboards requiring extensive brand immersion. We provide detailed quotes based on the specific content scope and deliverable requirements.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is included in your content creation training programs?',
    a: 'Training covers language AI tools (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini), prompt engineering by content type, workflow architecture, quality-control frameworks and hands-on workshops. Participants leave with practical content assets, reusable prompts and workflow templates.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you create content in multiple languages?',
    a: 'Yes. Major global languages with cultural adaptation beyond literal translation. The team includes native speakers who ensure messaging resonates locally while maintaining global brand consistency.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you ensure content accuracy and avoid AI hallucinations?',
    a: 'Every piece goes through human review by subject-matter experts. Fact-checking protocols, source verification and editorial oversight are built in. For technical or specialised content, we collaborate with your internal teams to validate accuracy.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What about SEO optimisation for AI-generated content?',
    a: 'SEO best practice is built into the content generation process: keyword integration, semantic relevance, content-structure optimisation and metadata. The content is designed to perform in both traditional search and emerging AI-powered search platforms.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can AI-generated content be used across all marketing channels?',
    a: 'Yes. All content meets platform requirements, maintains brand compliance and adapts to channel-specific formats. The content works across paid advertising, social media, websites, email and commerce platforms.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you handle content localisation for global markets?',
    a: 'We specialise in market-specific content adaptation that goes beyond translation: cultural nuance, local market preferences, platform requirements and regulatory compliance for each region the brand operates in.',
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};
---

<Layout
  title="AIGC Content Creation | AI Copywriting Studio | hubStudio"
  description="Studio-grade AI copywriting at hubStudio: campaign storyboards, e-commerce, email, SEO, naming and tone of voice, with human strategists leading every brief."
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <div class="prog" aria-hidden="true"><span class="prog__bar"></span></div>

  <div class="page">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero__panel">
        <svg class="hero__reg" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
          <path d="M50 4v92M4 50h92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
        </svg>
        <div class="hero__panel-in">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r">
            <span class="kicker__tick"></span>AI Production
            <span class="kicker__sep">/</span> Content
          </p>
          <h1 class="hero__title">
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i">A month of</span></span>
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i">content in</span></span>
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i serif">a day.</span></span>
          </h1>
          <p class="hero__tag r" style="--d:.45s">
            Strategic writers, <em>not just software</em>.
          </p>
          <div class="hero__lead r" style="--d:.55s">
            <p>
              Brand positioning cannot be automated. Audience insight
              requires human empathy. Creative direction shapes every
              line. AIGC executes faster and cheaper than traditional
              copywriting, but human intelligence still leads every word
              we write.
            </p>
            <p>
              The studio pairs content strategists and creative directors
              with custom language models trained on your brand. AI
              serves the narrative; it does not write it on its own.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__cta r" style="--d:.65s">
            <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Start a content brief</Button>
            <a class="ghost-link ghost-link--light" href="#lanes">
              See the work
              <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero__meta r" style="--d:.72s">
            Shanghai studio <span>/</span> Human strategists, AIGC execution
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__visual">
        <img
          src="/Images/aiprod-content-hero.jpg"
          alt="A daylit AIGC content production floor with a single strategist reviewing campaign copy variations on a calibrated monitor and printed editorial proofs pinned along the back wall, warm window light from camera left."
          width="1024"
          height="1024"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <span class="hero__chip">Shanghai <span>/</span> Content floor</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cbar" aria-hidden="true">
      {colourBar.map((c) => <span style={`background:${c}`}></span>)}
    </div>

    <section class="why">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="band band--split">
          <div>
            <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Why now</p>
            <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
              When strategic writing<br />meets <span class="serif">machine intelligence</span>.
            </h2>
          </div>
          <p class="band__note band__note--light r" style="--d:.1s">
            Production costs drop 60 to 80%. Budget moves from execution
            into strategy, testing and media. The team writes ten times
            the content without ten times the headcount. The model
            grows with the brief, not the org chart.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="reasons">
          {
            reasons.map((r, i) => (
              <article class="reason r" style={`--d:${i * 0.08}s`}>
                <p class="reason__label">
                  <span class="reason__tick"></span>
                  {r.label}
                </p>
                <h3 class="reason__title">{r.title}</h3>
                <p class="reason__body">{r.body}</p>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cover" id="lanes">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="band">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>What we write</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Three lanes of <span class="serif">content production</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="band__note r" style="--d:.1s">
            Brand and campaign, commercial and performance, strategic and
            naming. Each lane shares the same model training, the same
            voice guardrails and the same senior strategist sign-off.
          </p>
        </header>

        {
          lanes.map((c, i) => (
            <article class={`feature ${i % 2 === 1 ? 'feature--rev' : ''}`}>
              <figure class="feature__media crop r-clip">
                <div class="crop__inner">
                  <img
                    src={c.image}
                    alt={c.alt}
                    width="1024"
                    height="820"
                    loading="lazy"
                  />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="fig">{c.label}</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <div class="feature__body">
                <p class="feature__idx r">
                  <span class="feature__tick"></span>
                  Content lane
                </p>
                <h3 class="dh dh--sm r" style="--d:.05s">{c.heading}</h3>
                {c.lead && <p class="feature__lead r" style="--d:.1s">{c.lead}</p>}
                {c.body.map((para, pi) => (
                  <p class="feature__p r" style={`--d:${0.12 + pi * 0.06}s`}>
                    {para}
                  </p>
                ))}
                <p class="feature__scope r" style="--d:.24s">In scope</p>
                <ul class="chips r" style="--d:.28s">
                  {c.tags.map((t) => (
                    <li class="chip">{t}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="source">
      <div class="shell source__grid">
        <div class="source__visual">
          <figure class="source__main crop">
            <div class="crop__inner">
              <img
                src="/Images/hubstudio-shanghai-studio.webp"
                alt="A wide view of the hubStudio Shanghai floor with editorial daylight, calibrated stations and printed editorial proofs along the back wall."
                width="1024"
                height="820"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </figure>
          <div class="source__stat">
            <span class="source__stat-num">60 to 80%</span>
            <span class="source__stat-cap">Cost reduction versus traditional copywriting</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="source__body">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Why hubStudio</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Strategy first.<br />Technology <span class="serif">second</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="source__lead r" style="--d:.1s">
            AIGC generates text. It cannot craft a market position,
            define what makes a brand different, or understand the
            competitive landscape that shapes the message. Algorithms
            analyse data; strategists understand the emotional triggers,
            the cultural context and the human motivations that build
            brand loyalty.
          </p>
          <p class="source__p r" style="--d:.16s">
            Our strategists and creative directors guide every brief, so
            AI serves the narrative vision rather than producing generic
            copy that sounds like everyone else.
          </p>
          <p class="source__p r" style="--d:.22s">
            That positions the team at the front of rapidly evolving
            AI capability while building a content operation that
            survives the next model release rather than being rebuilt
            by it.
          </p>
          <ul class="creds r" style="--d:.28s">
            <li class="cred">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              Strategist sign-off
            </li>
            <li class="cred">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              Custom-trained models
            </li>
            <li class="cred">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              Native-speaker localisation
            </li>
            <li class="cred">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              NDA in place
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq">
      <div class="shell faq__grid">
        <aside class="faq__intro">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Questions</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Before the<br />first <span class="serif">draft</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="faq__sub r" style="--d:.1s">
            The questions content leads ask before we begin. If yours is
            not below, put it in the brief.
          </p>
          <div class="r" style="--d:.16s">
            <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Start a content brief</Button>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="acc">
          {
            faqs.map((faq) => (
              <div class="acc__row r">
                <button class="acc__q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                  <span class="acc__qmark">Q</span>
                  <span class="acc__qtext">{faq.q}</span>
                  <span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span></span><span></span>
                  </span>
                </button>
                <div class="acc__a">
                  <div class="acc__a-inner">
                    <p>{faq.a}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="end">
      <svg class="end__reg" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
        <path d="M50 4v92M4 50h92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
      </svg>
      <div class="shell end__inner">
        <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Build with us</p>
        <h2 class="end__title r" style="--d:.05s">
          Write at<br /><span class="serif">our pace</span>.
        </h2>
        <p class="end__p r" style="--d:.12s">
          Send a campaign brief, an editorial calendar or just the
          content gap you keep running into. A senior lead reads it
          inside two working days and replies with a phased plan, a
          cost shape and an honest read on which lane starts first.
        </p>
        <div class="end__cta r" style="--d:.18s">
          <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Start a content brief</Button>
          <a class="ghost-link ghost-link--light" href="/work">
            See client work
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cbar cbar--end" aria-hidden="true">
        {colourBar.map((c) => <span style={`background:${c}`}></span>)}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { --ink: #0e1633; --navy: #0e1f4e; --paper: #f0ede9; --paper-2: #e7e3dd; overflow: clip; }
  .shell { width: 100%; max-width: 1280px; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: clamp(22px, 5vw, 60px); }
  .prog { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto 0; height: 3px; z-index: 200; pointer-events: none; }
  .prog__bar { display: block; height: 100%; width: 100%; transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: 0 50%; background: var(--brand-orange); }
  .r, .r-clip { --d: 0s; }
  .r { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(26px); transition: opacity 0.7s ease, transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d); }
  .r.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .r-clip .crop__inner { clip-path: inset(0 0 101% 0); transition: clip-path 1.05s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .r-clip .crop__inner img { transform: scale(1.12); transition: transform 1.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .r-clip.in .crop__inner { clip-path: inset(0 0 0 0); }
  .r-clip.in .crop__inner img { transform: scale(1); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .r, .r.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
    .r-clip .crop__inner, .r-clip .crop__inner img { clip-path: none; transform: none; transition: none; }
  }
  .kicker { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .kicker--light { color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.66); }
  .kicker__tick { width: 22px; height: 0; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .kicker__sep { color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .dh { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.4vw, 62px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .dh--sm { font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 38px); }
  .serif { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop { position: relative; margin: 0; }
  .crop::before, .crop::after { content: ''; position: absolute; width: 16px; height: 16px; z-index: 2; }
  .crop::before { top: -9px; left: -9px; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); border-left: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop::after { right: -9px; bottom: 28px; border-right: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop__inner { overflow: hidden; border-radius: 4px; }
  .crop__inner img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .fig { margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .ghost-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-size: var(--type-small); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); }
  .ghost-link svg { width: 19px; height: 19px; transition: transform 0.24s ease-out; }
  .ghost-link:hover svg { transform: translateX(5px); }
  .ghost-link--light { color: var(--text-on-dark); }
  .band { max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 5vw, 70px); display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .band--split { max-width: none; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .band--split { grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.82fr; align-items: end; gap: 18px 60px; }
    .band--split > div { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  }
  .band__note { font-size: var(--type-lead); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .band__note--light { color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.76); }
  .cbar { display: flex; height: 12px; }
  .cbar span { flex: 1; }
  .cbar--end { margin-top: clamp(60px, 8vw, 110px); }
  .hero { display: grid; background: var(--ink); color: var(--text-on-dark); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .hero__panel { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; padding: clamp(40px, 4.4vw, 72px) clamp(24px, 5vw, 64px); overflow: clip; }
  .hero__reg { position: absolute; width: clamp(240px, 28vw, 420px); right: -12%; bottom: -14%; color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.055); pointer-events: none; }
  .hero__panel-in { position: relative; width: 100%; max-width: 600px; }
  .hero__title { margin-top: 24px; font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(40px, 5.6vw, 80px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.045em; }
  .hero__title .line { display: block; overflow: hidden; padding: 0.22em 0.14em; margin: -0.22em -0.14em; }
  .hero__title .line__i { display: block; transform: translateY(145%); transition: transform 0.9s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
  .hero__title .line:nth-child(1) .line__i { transition-delay: 0.12s; }
  .hero__title .line:nth-child(2) .line__i { transition-delay: 0.22s; }
